WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.501
A high stakes visit between

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.703
two powerful strategic partners

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:04.804
is being watched

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:05.672
around the world

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.439
for the first time

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.408
since Russia invaded Ukraine.

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:11.144
China's Xi Jinping is in Moscow meeting

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:13.413
with Russian President Vladimir Putin.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:14.314
Ukraine is, of course,

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:16.383
expected to top the agenda.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.550
Three day trip

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.285
with Beijing framing itself

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.987
as a peacemaker.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:21.321
Mr.

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.722
Xi says that China will work

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.924
with Russia to, in his words,

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:28.828
safeguard the international order.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.196
It is true

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.498
that both of our countries

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.767
share the same or similar goals,

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.470
we have exerted efforts

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.605
for the prosperity

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:40.673
of our respective countries.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.276
Clearly, we can cooperate and work

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.478
together to achieve our goals

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.382
The meeting comes just days

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.051
after the International Criminal Court

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:53.153
issued an arrest warrant for Vladimir

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.588
Putin on war crimes charges.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:56.689
Just walk us through what

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.691
Xi Jinping at this point needs

00:00:58.691 --> 00:00:59.259
from Russia.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.397
Well, Xi Jinping, I mean, by

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.598
traveling to Russia

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:06.766
just after securing

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:07.901
this unprecedented

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.036
third presidential term,

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.404
he's making very clear.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.173
He's sending a message

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.441
to the west, to the world

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.209
where his priorities lie.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.777
And even though,

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:18.211
you know,

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.979
his economic relationship

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.381
with the United States

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.148
and NATO

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:24.851
is hugely important in terms of dollars,

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.853
that's not Xi's priority.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.822
His priority is ideology.

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:31.024
And he and Vladimir Putin share

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:33.660
the belief that the world order

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.896
as it has existed for the last 70 years,

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:38.331
you know, insured

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.732
by the United States,

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.669
is a world order that needs to change.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.170
They believe

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.072
that the system of democracy,

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.141
the cultural liberalism,

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.343
is is a disgrace.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.412
And they want to see the world

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.980
aligned more in the way

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:54.981
that their countries are,

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.650
where they are controlled very heavily

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:58.985
by the government.

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.086
And so

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:00.720
this is

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.889
a bigger issue for President

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:04.824
Xi than just Vladimir Putin's,

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:05.225
you know,

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:05.925
war crimes

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:06.359
charges

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.594
in the International Criminal Court,

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.863
bigger than the war in Ukraine itself.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.331
This is about,

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:14.167
you know,
combining the powers of these two nuclear

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.503
armed authoritarian superpowers

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.073
and using using that combined power

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.909
to shape the course of

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.511
of the world order for,

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.812
you know, for the future.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.413
They both believe that this is their

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.748
this is their mission.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.583
And so you know, this meeting,

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.751
these three days,

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:32.418
the decisions

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:32.919
that they make,

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:33.753
the conversations

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:34.988
that they have seemed

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:37.157
to be solidifying this,

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:38.158
as they've called it, there

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:41.861
no limits partnership And and you see

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:42.529
Xi Jinping

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.597
trying to show China's,

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.766
you know, China's force,

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:48.902
not only militarily and economically,

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.069
but also

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.471
in diplomacy, brokering

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.373
that peace deal in the Middle East

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:55.575
recently between Saudi Arabia and Iran

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:58.111
and making sure that that deal,

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.512
none of the official documents

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.980
would be in English.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.081
This is

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.783
this is what she has always

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:06.119
felt is an inevitable

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:08.254
revival and rise of China.

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:10.790
And he does not want the United States

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.059
and the West standing in in that way.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:17.397
Now, an embarrassing defeat in Ukraine

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.098
for the West

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:19.799
is not something

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.334
that would disappoint Xi Jinping.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.503
So that is why there's growing concern

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:24.170
that he's

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:27.073
considering these arming of lethal,

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.575
lethal weapons, ammunition

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:29.409
because we know that

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:30.043
the US believes

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:30.977
that Russia

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:33.046
might not have any serviceable ammunition

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.080
before the end of this year.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.949
That's
something that China can help them with,

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.684
along with microchips

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.752
and other other types of weapons.

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.621
That could really change the course

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.623
for Russian soldiers on the battlefield.

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.091
So what happens over

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.726
the next few days of discussion, Zain,

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.828
is going to have huge

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:50.964
huge ramifications for the war in Ukraine

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.232
and beyond.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.767
We'll see what happens.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.135
I'm sure you'll be watching that very,

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.170
very closely.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.137
Will Ripley live for us there.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.105
Thank you so much.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:03:59.639
It's time now

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:00.573
for the exchange

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.775
and a conversation with your son.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.077
She's a senior fellow

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.778
and co-director of China

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.013
at the Stimson Center,

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.615
a Washington think tank.

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:11.150
Thank you so much for being with us.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.386
Just walk us through at this point

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:15.188
why you think

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.423
Russia needs China and vice versa.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:20.893
Thank you very much for having me.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.929
I think the reason why Russia needs

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.964
China is this point is quite clear.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.633
Russia has been under severe

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:27.800
international sanctions

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.435
since the beginning of the war,

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.970
and its economic partners

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.071
on the international market

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.107
has become increasingly limited

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.808
as a source of foreign funding,

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:36.976
especially investment

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.611
has also become limited.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.712
China is China.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.581
China is Russia's largest neighbor.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.850
And China also shares its anti-U.S.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.785
agenda with with Russia.

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.920
So evidently China has appeared

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:50.723
what emerged as one of the few partners

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.992
that Russia comes to rely on

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:55.328
in this precarious condition.

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:56.095
The imports

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.497
from the Chinese perspective,

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:58.765
I think the most important

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:01.100
consideration remains to be geopolitics

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.635
and about geopolitics.

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:03.770
The Chinese would mean

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:04.771
while the

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.072
great power competition

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:07.273
or the strategic competition

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:08.408
with the United States,

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:09.409
no matter what,

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:10.143
and regardless

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.145
of the result of the war in Ukraine.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:13.680
China sees Russia

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.681
as a partner,

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.783
as a as a partner, as shares

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:18.117
the same vision

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.352
about the need

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.654
to counter the US hegemony in the world.

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:23.956
So that geopolitical instinct

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.591
really dictates China's

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.659
behavior at this point.

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:29.595
So does China's

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.631
sort of cozying up to Russia.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:32.432
How much does it

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.466
affect China's

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:34.801
relationship with its European

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.270
trading partners, do you think?

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.105
I think it does affect with China's

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:40.440
relationship with Europe,

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.841
not only in terms of trade,

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.843
but also in terms of the diplomacy

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:46.079
and also in terms of the political optics

00:05:46.079 --> 00:05:47.480
and the European concern

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.247
about China

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.082
aligning itself

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:49.949
with Russia

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:50.917
and the implications

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.919
it would have for the war in Ukraine,

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:53.553
which is why

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.088
I think
the Chinese are trying

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:57.523
to frame this present China

00:05:57.724 --> 00:05:59.092
as a peace broker

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:01.194
instead of a Russia accomplice

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:03.096
through this sort of this trip.

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:05.164
So we saw that China made the proposal

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:05.732
on the peace

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:07.667
settlement of the Ukraine crisis

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:08.868
about a month ago.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.403
And then earlier in March,

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:10.770
China

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.206
also facilitated the peace deal

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:14.874
between Iran and Saudi.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.943
So all these are giving the

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:18.378
international community,

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:19.979
I would say, an illusion

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:21.848
that China is now going to emerge

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.049
as a great mediator

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:24.450
between Russia and Ukraine,

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.351
which I don't think

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:26.986
is the primary goal of this trip.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:27.987
And I don't think it is

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:29.489
within China's capacity

00:06:29.489 --> 00:06:31.724
to mediate the peace for the Ukraine war.

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:36.362
Do you anticipate I mean, obviously,

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:37.597
Zelensky,

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:39.766
I'm sure, would want to speak to Xi

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:40.733
Jinping. Can you.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.001
Do you anticipate

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:42.969
any sort of situation

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:43.970
where the coming days

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:44.537
Xi Jinping

00:06:44.537 --> 00:06:46.906
ends up speaking to President Zelensky?

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:50.543
Indeed, I think that's very well

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:53.045
speculated, and that's very possibly

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:53.513
to be

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:54.213
to be happening

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:56.282
after Xi Jinping's trip to Moscow.

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:56.916
And remember,

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:58.418
whether the Chinese are trying to do

00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:01.721
is to frame or present China as a broker.

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:02.755
So therefore,

00:07:02.755 --> 00:07:04.457
they want to present a case

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:05.925
obviously jumping, conducting

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:06.993
shadow diplomacy

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:08.694
between Russia and Ukraine.

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:10.696
So Xi Jinping meeting was putting first

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:12.632
and then having a virtual phone call

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:13.933
or a real phone call,

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:15.868
whereas with President Zelensky,

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:18.037
it will give China that image

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:19.338
of being the broker

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:20.139
conducting shuttle

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:21.441
diplomacy between the two.

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.210
You mentioned that China doesn't

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.578
really have the capacity per

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.880
se to sort of broker a real peace deal.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:31.684
But just explain to us how much China's

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:33.219
position on the world

00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:35.555
stage has been bolstered

00:07:35.555 --> 00:07:36.789
by the sort of position

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:37.590
that it's carving out

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:40.126
for itself in this war.

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:43.196
Look, there are pros and cons.

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:45.398
There are costs to China's position,

00:07:45.398 --> 00:07:47.200
and there are also some benefits

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.969
to China's position in terms of the cost.

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:51.170
And most importantly,

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:53.473
I was a China understands that

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:56.943
its pro-Russia neutrality is taking great

00:07:57.143 --> 00:07:58.711
as doing great damage

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:00.613
to China's relationship with the West

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:01.380
including both

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.882
the United States and Europe.

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:04.183
And it also frames China

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:05.585
as a dishonest broker

00:08:05.585 --> 00:08:06.919
or dishonest a player

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:07.954
in this whole thing.

00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:09.121
When China presented

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.189
as peace settlement

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:12.391
proposal on February 24th,

00:08:12.391 --> 00:08:15.495
most people are underwhelmed by how empty

00:08:15.495 --> 00:08:16.996
and how little substance

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:17.930
the deal actually

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.832
or the proposal actually offers.

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:21.200
So that's not necessarily

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:21.667
going to do

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:22.702
China more favor

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:24.704
in terms of his great power diplomacy.

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:26.105
But on the other hand,

00:08:26.105 --> 00:08:28.007
I think the Chinese also see benefits

00:08:28.007 --> 00:08:29.642
associated with this,

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:30.810
whereas this ambiguity

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.012
in terms of the Russian war for Ukraine,

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:34.280
because for a lot of

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.581
the Chinese strategists,

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:37.583
if the Chinese don't take a position.

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.752
So every country and all parties to

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:40.419
the conflict

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:42.488
will want to gain China's favor.

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:45.391
They will want to gain China

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.193
to support their position.

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:49.262
So I think there is also this argument

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:51.564
that the China should remain neutral

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:52.365
or should remain

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:54.734
non-committal in terms of is it

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.402
in terms of its position.

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:57.403
Last but not least,

00:08:57.403 --> 00:08:59.005
remember, for the Chinese

00:08:59.005 --> 00:08:59.906
the most important

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:00.540
foreign policy

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.908
consideration is always going

00:09:01.908 --> 00:09:03.342
to be the United States.

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:04.143
So when they think

00:09:04.143 --> 00:09:05.978
about the Indo-Pacific strategy

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:07.280
and the strategic competition

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.347
with the United States,

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:10.383
I think the first question that emerges

00:09:10.383 --> 00:09:11.884
is that while U.S.

00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:13.953
is no longer distracted in Ukraine,

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.322
then how much more attention

00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:17.990
and how much more resources U.S.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.959
